; Each frame's filters. Per segment nine cards in (n, c, ma, mb, uon, vm, gl, cf, af), per frame three (j, u,
; end); per frame four cards out to glide (a, b, uu, g) and two to the level (snd, V, OUT at ls and lv). A frame
; j < c is the closure: filter cf, sounding if cf is a voice bar, else silent (snd 0, or 9 at the very end). Frame 0
; of a segment with af is aspirated: af, unvoiced. Any other frame speaks through ma to mb (by u if uon), voiced if
; vm, with glides if gl.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            seg     INP   i        03-15: a segment (i counts its frames down)
  04                    INP   c
  05                    INP   ma
  06                    INP   mb
  07                    INP   uon
  08                    INP   vm
  09                    INP   gl
  10                    INP   cf
  11                    INP   af
  12            frm     CLA   i
  13                    SUB   00
  14                    TAC   seg
  15                    STO   i
  16            fj      INP   j        16-31: a frame: the closure, the aspirated frame or the rest
  17            fu      INP   u
  18            fe      INP   e
  19                    CLA   z
  20                    STO   g
  21                    STO   uu
  22                    CLA   00
  23                    STO   snd
  24                    STO   v
  25                    CLA   j
  26                    SUB   c
  27                    TAC   clo
  28                    CLA   j
  29                    SUB   00
  30                    TAC   j0
  31                    JMP   norm
  32            j0      CLA   af       32-40: aspirated
  33                    SUB   00
  34                    TAC   norm
  35                    CLA   af
  36                    STO   a
  37                    STO   b
  38                    CLA   z
  39                    STO   v
  40                    JMP   out
  41            clo     CLA   cf       41-54: the closure
  42                    STO   a
  43                    STO   b
  44                    SUB   00
  45                    TAC   sil
  46                    JMP   out
  47            sil     CLA   z
  48                    STO   snd
  49                    CLA   e
  50                    SUB   00
  51                    TAC   out
  52                    CLA   c9
  53                    STO   snd
  54                    JMP   out
  55            norm    CLA   ma       55-67: the rest
  56                    STO   a
  57                    CLA   mb
  58                    STO   b
  59                    CLA   vm
  60                    STO   v
  61                    CLA   gl
  62                    STO   g
  63                    CLA   uon
  64                    SUB   00
  65                    TAC   out
  66                    CLA   u
  67                    STO   uu
  68            out     OUT   a        68-94: the cards
  69                    OUT   b
  70                    OUT   uu
  71                    OUT   g
  72            ls      OUT   snd
  73            lv      OUT   v
  74                    JMP   frm
  75            c       DATA  0
  76            ma      DATA  0
  77            mb      DATA  0
  78            uon     DATA  0
  79            vm      DATA  0
  80            gl      DATA  0
  81            cf      DATA  0
  82            af      DATA  0
  83            i       DATA  0
  84            j       DATA  0
  85            u       DATA  0
  86            e       DATA  0
  87            a       DATA  0
  88            b       DATA  0
  89            uu      DATA  0
  90            g       DATA  0
  91            snd     DATA  0
  92            v       DATA  0
  93            z       DATA  0
  94            c9      DATA  9
